and Molecular Biology PhD Students\nHistopathology\nCurriculum\nHistopathology Faculty\nMS Histopathology Alumni\nMolecular Cell Biology and Neuroscience\nCurriculum\nMCBN Faculty\nNeuroscience\nDoctoral Program\nCurriculum\nFrequently Asked Questions\nProgram Alumni\nDO-PhD Program\nCurriculum\nProgram Alumni\nNeuroscience Faculty\nCurrent Neuroscience PhD Students\nTranslational Orthopedic Device Engineering & Science\nMaster's Program\nMTODE Program Alumni\nCertificate Program\nFaculty and Guest Lecturers\nRequest More Information\nTranslational Research\nDoctoral Fellows\nAbout Rowan-Virtua TBES\nTBES Leadership\nGraduate Program Faculty at TBES\nTBES Campus Information\nSummer Research Opportunities\nHigh School Biomedical Scholars Program\nRISER Summer Program\nSummer Undergraduate Research Experience\nStudent Resources\nRegistrar\nRegistration\nForms\nAcademic Advising\nStudent Organizations\nDoctoral Grant Opportunities\nCareer and Professional Development Services\nAccessibility Services for TBES/SOM\nHealth & Wellness Resources for TBES/SOM Students\nCenter for Neurodiversity\nStudent Seminars & Professional Development Workshops\nHope Brings Strength Health Sciences Library\nHandbooks and Catalogs\nPolicies\nUniversity Wellness Center\nFrequently Asked Questions\nHome\n/\nAdmissions and Aid /\nAdmissions /\nFrequently Asked Questions\nTBES Admissions FAQ\nThe admissions process can be daunting. To help you get the answers you need, we have compiled a list of our most frequently asked questions.\nIf you have additional questions that are not answered below, please contact us. We are excited to hear from you and look forward to helping you make the best decisions for your future.\nHow do I check the status of my application?\nOnce you submit your application to Rowan-Virtua TBES, you can log into your application status portal at any time to review the status of your application.\nIf you have not yet applied, but are starting to send items such as test scores or transcripts, we recommend submitting your application as soon as possible. The process of tracking and confirming if we have received documents is seamless with a submitted application.\nIf you have any questions, please contact us: tbesadmissions@rowan.edu.\nCan I fax my transcripts and/or letters of recommendation?\nNo, we cannot accept faxed transcripts or letters of recommendation. All transcripts must be official and therefore sent directly from the issuing institution. Some schools participate in electronic submission of official transcripts which can be sent to electronic-transcripts@rowan.edu directly from the issuing school. Letters of recommendation can be submitted through the application status portal.\nI have a degree from another country, do I need to submit a credential evaluation, such as a WES?\nYes, students with credentials from a foreign institution must have that credential evaluated by a NACES-approved evaluating agency at the time of application. Evaluation must indicate that the student has earned the equivalent of at least a U.S. Bachelor\u2019s degree. Visit the NACES site for more information.\nIs there housing on campus?\nNo, there is no on-campus housing. However, there are many affordable apartment complexes within walking distance. Please view the SOM off-campus housing page for additional information.\nI am an international student, to which programs can I apply?\nInternational students are eligible to apply for any TBES program. However, a student visa cannot be issued for any certificate or distance learning programs.\nCopyright \u00a92026. All Rights Reserved.\nConsumer Disclosures.\nTranslational Biomedical Engineering and Sciences Twitter\nTranslational Biomedical Engineering and Sciences Facebook\nTranslational Biomedical Engineering and Sciences Instagram\nContact Us\nRowan University\nVirtua Health\nNotice of Availability of Rowan's Annual Security & Fire Safety Report", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://www.ro